<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Kansas harvest in full flow.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Kansas harvest in full flow.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harvesting of hard red winter wheat was in full flow in Kansas on Wednesday with only a shortage of custom cutters limiting progress, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;They will be going very strong today and tomorrow for sure,&quot; one Kansas dealer said, noting producers wanted to get as much wheat as possible harvested ahead of forecast rains set to enter the state late Thursday.</p>
<p>One dealer estimated that at the current rate, up to 10 percent of the Kansas crop could be harvested in a single day.</p>
<p>Most dealers reported slow farmer selling after the recent slide in prices to the lowest level in about three years.</p>
<p>One Oklahoma dealer, however, said cash flow needs were forcing many farmers to offload wheat.</p>
<p>&quot;They (farmers) are selling quite a bit. They have to pay the bills,&quot; one dealer said.</p>
<p>Basis bids were holding mostly steady.  </p>
